                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91a53c61-9c80-4dcf-812c-1c58590f2c2e",
                                "sense_id": "ef80e5e4-ef92-32ef-968a-18039aba28f4",
                                "text": "Treatment options for symptomatic cholelithiasis include surgery, dissolution with oral bile salt litholytics or contact solvents, and current fragmentation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03f7fb1c-e84a-4e35-9595-1dfa55743cb4",
                                "sense_id": "ef80e5e4-ef92-32ef-968a-18039aba28f4",
                                "text": "Accordingly, citric acid, a calcium chelator, was selected as a pancreatic litholytic, and a 50-mg pancreatic stone was dissolved in vitro after 25 days ina solution of 3.9 mM/L citric acid, corresponding to a concentration of 749 μg/mL in the pancreatic juice following injection of citric acid into the canine duodenum."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12ab39eb-7e5f-4a3e-b24f-ae9c53cbf7f2",
                                "sense_id": "ef80e5e4-ef92-32ef-968a-18039aba28f4",
                                "text": "Phyllanthus niuri (chanca piedra) herb is a traditional litholytic; its Spanish common name translates as “stone breaker.”"
